Yes, but copyright law and trademark law are two different things.
Names in general don't fall under copyright law[1].

The NGPL covers the part of the authorship rights[2] but not the part
about branding.

There are licenses that also set forth conditions on what you have to
do with the name of a forked project. For example previous versions of
the LaTeX Project Public License stated that you have to change the
name of a package if you modify it (because of concerns about
incompatibilities).

Bye
